<title>USA: Moore takes Q4 charges, sees more in Q1.</title>
<headline>Moore takes Q4 charges, sees more in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRITAIN, Conn. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moore Medical Corp said on Tuesday that it took fourth quarter charges of $2.6 million after-tax or $0.90 per share and expects to take further charges in the first half of 1997 of $528,000 or $0.18 per share.</p>
<p>It said the charges relate to supply contracts with federal agencies.</p>
<p>Moore said it filed its form 10-K for 1996 with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission after a two-week delay in order to finalize the fourth quarter charges.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
